<Layout
	title="Double Right Triangle Problems | Applications of Trigonometry | Class 10 | The Concepts Adda"
	description="Master complex 2-triangle NCERT word problems (moving ships/cars, pedestals, balloons, dual angle observations) for Class 10 Mathematics."
>
	<main class="lesson-page">
		<div class="lesson-container">
			<a href="/applications-of-trigonometry" class="back-link">
				<span class="back-arrow">←</span>
				<span>Back to Applications of Trigonometry</span>
			</a>

			<!-- LESSON HEADER -->
			<section class="lesson-header">
				<div class="lesson-number">03</div>
				<div class="lesson-header-copy">
					<div class="lesson-label">LESSON 03 · CLASS 10 MATHEMATICS (NCERT)</div>
					<h1>Double Right <span>Triangle Problems</span></h1>
					<p>
						Master complex NCERT word problems involving two right-angled triangles: moving objects, pedestals, balloons, and dual angle observations.
					</p>
				</div>
			</section>

			<!-- CONTENT LAYOUT -->
			<section class="content-layout">
				<article class="lesson-content">

					<!-- 01 · GENERAL APPROACH FOR 2 TRIANGLES -->
					<div class="topic-label">01 · SOLVING APPROACH</div>
					<h2>Method for Double Triangle Questions</h2>

					<div class="summary-list">
						<div class="summary-item">
							<span>Step 1</span>
							<p>Identify the <strong>two right-angled triangles</strong> sharing a common side (or base).</p>
						</div>
						<div class="summary-item">
							<span>Step 2</span>
							<p>Write <strong>tan θ₁</strong> for the smaller triangle and <strong>tan θ₂</strong> for the larger triangle.</p>
						</div>
						<div class="summary-item">
							<span>Step 3</span>
							<p>Express the common side from equation 1 and substitute into equation 2 to solve!</p>
						</div>
					</div>

					<!-- 02 · SOLVED NCERT EXAMPLES -->
					<div class="topic-label second-label">02 · SOLVED NCERT EXAMPLES</div>
					<h2>Step-by-Step Problem Solving</h2>

					<!-- Example 1 -->
					<div class="example-card">
						<div class="example-header">
							<span class="example-badge">EXAMPLE 1 · STATUE ON PEDESTAL</span>
							<h3>A 1.6 m tall statue stands on top of a pedestal. From a point on ground, elevation of top of statue is 60° and top of pedestal is 45°. Find height of pedestal.</h3>
						</div>
						<div class="example-solution">
							<!-- SVG Diagram -->
							<div style="margin:15px 0; text-align:center;">
								<svg width="360" height="230" viewBox="0 0 360 230" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" style="background:#f8fafc; border-radius:18px; border:1px solid #cbd5e1; box-shadow:0 6px 20px rgba(0,0,0,0.03);">
									<!-- Ground Line -->
									<line x1="30" y1="190" x2="330" y2="190" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="2"/>
									<!-- Pedestal h (Vertical) -->
									<line x1="280" y1="110" x2="280" y2="190" stroke="#0f172a" stroke-width="3.5"/>
									<!-- Statue 1.6 m (Vertical Top) -->
									<line x1="280" y1="40" x2="280" y2="110" stroke="#2563eb" stroke-width="3.5"/>

									<!-- Line of sight to pedestal top C (45°) -->
									<line x1="50" y1="190" x2="280" y2="110" stroke="#059669" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-dasharray="4,4"/>
									<!-- Line of sight to statue top D (60°) -->
									<line x1="50" y1="190" x2="280" y2="40" stroke="#dc2626" stroke-width="2.5"/>

									<!-- Right Angle Symbol -->
									<path d="M 268,190 L 268,178 L 280,178" stroke="#0f172a" stroke-width="1.5" fill="none"/>

									<!-- Angle Arcs -->
									<!-- 45° Arc -->
									<path d="M 90 190 A 40 40 0 0 0 85 178" stroke="#059669" stroke-width="2" fill="none"/>
									<text x="94" y="184" fill="#059669" font-size="11" font-weight="900">45°</text>

									<!-- 60° Arc -->
									<path d="M 110 190 A 60 60 0 0 0 102 159" stroke="#dc2626" stroke-width="2.5" fill="none"/>
									<text x="114" y="172" fill="#dc2626" font-size="12" font-weight="900">60°</text>

									<!-- Points -->
									<circle cx="50" cy="190" r="4.5" fill="#0f172a"/>
									<circle cx="280" cy="190" r="4.5" fill="#0f172a"/>
									<circle cx="280" cy="110" r="4.5" fill="#059669"/>
									<circle cx="280" cy="40" r="4.5" fill="#2563eb"/>

									<!-- Labels -->
									<text x="35" y="210" fill="#0f172a" font-size="14" font-weight="900">A (Observer)</text>
									<text x="285" y="210" fill="#0f172a" font-size="14" font-weight="900">B (Foot)</text>
									<text x="288" y="115" fill="#059669" font-size="13" font-weight="900">C (Pedestal Top)</text>
									<text x="288" y="38" fill="#2563eb" font-size="13" font-weight="900">D (Statue Top)</text>
									<text x="150" y="210" fill="#0f172a" font-size="13" font-weight="800">x</text>
									<text x="290" y="155" fill="#059669" font-size="13" font-weight="800">h = ?</text>
									<text x="290" y="78" fill="#2563eb" font-size="13" font-weight="800">1.6 m</text>
								</svg>
							</div>

							<p>Let height of pedestal = <em>h</em>, distance from observer = <em>x</em>. Height of top of statue = <em>h + 1.6</em>.</p>
							<p><strong>In smaller △ (for pedestal):</strong></p>
							<div class="calc-box">
								tan 45° = h / x ⟹ 1 = h / x ⟹ <strong>x = h</strong>
							</div>

							<p style="margin-top:14px;"><strong>In larger △ (for statue + pedestal):</strong></p>
							<div class="calc-box">
								tan 60° = (h + 1.6) / x<br/>
								√3 = (h + 1.6) / h &nbsp;(since x = h)<br/>
								h√3 = h + 1.6 ⟹ h(√3 - 1) = 1.6<br/>
								<strong>h = 1.6 / (√3 - 1) = 0.8(√3 + 1) metres</strong>
							</div>
							<p style="margin-top:10px;">Height of pedestal is <strong>0.8(√3 + 1) m</strong> (≈ 2.18 m).</p>
						</div>
					</div>

					<!-- Example 2 -->
					<div class="example-card">
						<div class="example-header">
							<span class="example-badge">EXAMPLE 2 · LIGHTHOUSE & SHIPS</span>
							<h3>As observed from top of 75 m high lighthouse, angles of depression of two ships are 30° and 45°. One ship is directly behind other. Find distance between ships.</h3>
						</div>
						<div class="example-solution">
							<!-- SVG Diagram -->
							<div style="margin:15px 0; text-align:center;">
								<svg width="380" height="230" viewBox="0 0 380 230" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" style="background:#f8fafc; border-radius:18px; border:1px solid #cbd5e1; box-shadow:0 6px 20px rgba(0,0,0,0.03);">
									<!-- Top Horizontal Line -->
									<line x1="30" y1="40" x2="310" y2="40" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="2" stroke-dasharray="4,4"/>
									<!-- Sea Level Ground Line -->
									<line x1="30" y1="190" x2="350" y2="190" stroke="#0284c7" stroke-width="2"/>

									<!-- Lighthouse 75 m (Vertical) -->
									<line x1="310" y1="40" x2="310" y2="190" stroke="#0f172a" stroke-width="4"/>

									<!-- Line of sight to Ship 1 (45°) -->
									<line x1="310" y1="40" x2="190" y2="190" stroke="#059669" stroke-width="2.5"/>
									<!-- Line of sight to Ship 2 (30°) -->
									<line x1="310" y1="40" x2="60" y2="190" stroke="#dc2626" stroke-width="2.5"/>

									<!-- Right Angle Symbol -->
									<path d="M 298,190 L 298,178 L 310,178" stroke="#0f172a" stroke-width="1.5" fill="none"/>

									<!-- Angle Arcs at Top L(310, 40) -->
									<!-- 30° Depression Arc -->
									<path d="M 255 40 A 55 55 0 0 0 262 67" stroke="#dc2626" stroke-width="2.5" fill="none"/>
									<text x="210" y="32" fill="#dc2626" font-size="12" font-weight="900">30°</text>

									<!-- 45° Depression Arc -->
									<path d="M 270 40 A 40 40 0 0 0 282 68" stroke="#059669" stroke-width="2" fill="none"/>
									<text x="250" y="54" fill="#059669" font-size="11" font-weight="900">45°</text>

									<!-- Ships (Circles) -->
									<circle cx="190" cy="190" r="5" fill="#059669"/>
									<circle cx="60" cy="190" r="5" fill="#dc2626"/>
									<circle cx="310" cy="40" r="5" fill="#0f172a"/>
									<circle cx="310" cy="190" r="5" fill="#0f172a"/>

									<!-- Labels -->
									<text x="175" y="210" fill="#059669" font-size="13" font-weight="900">Ship 1</text>
									<text x="45" y="210" fill="#dc2626" font-size="13" font-weight="900">Ship 2</text>
									<text x="315" y="38" fill="#0f172a" font-size="13" font-weight="900">Lighthouse Top</text>
									<text x="315" y="195" fill="#0f172a" font-size="13" font-weight="900">Foot</text>
									<text x="320" y="115" fill="#0f172a" font-size="13" font-weight="800">75 m</text>
									<text x="235" y="210" fill="#059669" font-size="12" font-weight="800">x</text>
									<text x="115" y="210" fill="#dc2626" font-size="12" font-weight="800">y = ?</text>
								</svg>
							</div>

							<p>Let height of lighthouse = 75 m. Distance to first ship = <em>x</em>, distance between ships = <em>y</em>.</p>
							<p><strong>In smaller △ (Ship 1):</strong></p>
							<div class="calc-box">
								tan 45° = 75 / x ⟹ 1 = 75 / x ⟹ <strong>x = 75 m</strong>
							</div>

							<p style="margin-top:14px;"><strong>In larger △ (Ship 2):</strong></p>
							<div class="calc-box">
								tan 30° = 75 / (x + y)<br/>
								1 / √3 = 75 / (75 + y)<br/>
								75 + y = 75√3 ⟹ <strong>y = 75(√3 - 1) metres</strong>
							</div>
							<p style="margin-top:10px;">Distance between the two ships is <strong>75(√3 - 1) m</strong> (≈ 54.9 m).</p>
						</div>
					</div>

					<!-- 03 · QUICK SUMMARY -->
					<div class="topic-label second-label">03 · QUICK SUMMARY</div>
					<h2>Key Takeaways</h2>

					<div class="summary-list">
						<div class="summary-item">
							<span>01</span>
							<p>Always solve the <strong>45° triangle first</strong> (since tan 45° = 1 makes Height = Distance!).</p>
						</div>
						<div class="summary-item">
							<span>02</span>
							<p>Substitute the 45° relation into the 30° or 60° triangle equation.</p>
						</div>
						<div class="summary-item">
							<span>03</span>
							<p>As an observer moves closer to a tower, the angle of elevation <strong>increases</strong> (30° ➔ 45° ➔ 60°).</p>
						</div>
					</div>

